Fill the entire background with one flat, uniform, fully opaque pure magenta, RGB 255 0 255, hex #FF00FF, edge to edge. The background must be that exact single colour and nothing else: no grey-and-white checkerboard pattern, no white, no grey, no gradient, no texture, no vignette, no ground plane, no cast shadow, no glow or halo bleeding into it. Magenta appears nowhere on the subject itself. Use a square canvas.

The attached first reference image is the finalized, approved base pose of this tree-golem guardian character (body proportions, block shapes, leaf clusters, palette, eyes, and overall body scale relative to the canvas are all final and correct). Redraw the exact same character at the moment of impact of a punch, mid-punch, arm fully extended forward -- NOT winding up, NOT cocked back, NOT a raised fist, NOT a ready-to-punch stance.

The right arm is fully extended straight out in front of the body, at the moment of impact: the fist is a full arm's length away from the torso, out at the right side of the canvas, as far from the body as the arm's own length allows. The shoulder follows the arm forward and the torso leans and twists into the punch. The left arm swings back behind the body for counter-balance, opposite to the extended right arm. The stance widens for balance, weight shifted onto the forward leg.

Do not change: the head shape or size, the leaf clusters (same clusters, same shapes, same positions relative to the body), the block/seam construction of the torso and legs, the palette (bark wood #6B4A2F / #8A6239 / #4A3220, leaves #B8CE59 / #9DA74D / #768738 / #384823), the two dark oval eyes with one highlight each looking right, or the overall body scale and proportions. Do not make the body smaller, larger, or shift its overall size relative to the canvas compared to the reference image -- match the reference's body scale exactly, only re-posing the arms, torso lean/twist, and stance.

A few small leaf fragments may fly off at the fist's point of impact (out at the extended arm's fist, near the right edge of the canvas) -- keep them fully inside the canvas, not cut off at the edge.

The body must fill the canvas the same way the reference image does: feet near the bottom edge, head/leaf-canopy near the top edge, standing height nearly filling the square canvas top to bottom. The fully extended arm and fist will naturally push the content wider toward the right side of the canvas -- that added width from the extended arm is expected and correct, do not shrink the body to compensate for it.

Render in the same 2.5D cut-paper faceted style as the reference: large flat polygonal facet planes, one flat solid color per plane, hard sharp creases between planes, three value bands (upper-left highlight, mid-tone base, lower-right shadow) per material, no smooth 3D shading, no gloss, no texture, no glow, no outer contour line. Three-quarter camera, facing right, matching the reference exactly.

No text, no letters, no frame, no card border, no watermark, no logo, no scene, no ground plane props, no ember or spark scatter, no motion blur, no glowing eye, no wind-up pose, no cocked-back fist, no raised fist, no ready-to-punch stance.
